# Testing and security rules

- Validate only the checks that are actually available and runnable.
- For frontend work, prefer formatting, linting, type checking, and tests where those commands exist.
- For backend work, prefer Python linting, testing, and relevant migration checks if available.
- For approval, tenant-boundary, or agent-scope changes, validate the permission model and evidence trail instead of assuming the logic is safe.
- Never weaken security controls to satisfy tests or a convenience requirement.
- If a test cannot run, document the exact reason and do not substitute an assumed pass result.
- Keep secrets and customer data out of prompts, errors, and generated artifacts.
